<title>USA: ACC Consumer files $20 mln in notes.</title>
<headline>ACC Consumer files $20 mln in notes.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>ACC Consumer Finance Corp filed on Friday with the Securities and Exchange Commission for up to $20 million in subordinated notes due 2003.</p>
<p>Net proceeds will be contributed to the company's secured financing facilities for use in part to repay temporarily a subordinated debt facility and for the company's general working capital purposes.</p>
<p>The offering will be made through McDonald &amp; Co and J.C. Bradford &amp; Co.</p>
</text>
